<title>INDIA: Indian sugar prices rise on scattered arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian sugar prices rise on scattered arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian sugar prices rose modestly on Monday on scattered arrivals and limited offerings by mill owners, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the ready delivery sugar S-30 rose by five rupees at 1,270/1,318 rupees while M-30 rose by 10 rupees at 1,300/1,360 rupees per quintal. Sugar mill delivery climbed up by 10 rupees to 1,220/1,230 rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
